  "body": "Building the `enforce_on_key_configs` dynamic block from a map keyed by `enforce_on_key_type` fails with `Duplicate object key` at plan time when a rule uses the same key type more than once. Cloud Armor explicitly permits repeating `HTTP_HEADER` and `HTTP_COOKIE` key types (up to three keys per rule, see [rate limiting overview](https://cloud.google.com/armor/docs/rate-limiting-overview)), so this made valid multi-key configurations unusable.\n\nThis change iterates the list directly in all eight dynamic blocks (root module and regional submodule), and updates the `throttle_project_droptwenty` rule in both affected examples to exercise a repeated `HTTP_HEADER` key type, with matching integration test assertions.\n\nNote on ordering: blocks were previously emitted sorted lexically by key type (an artifact of the map keying); they now follow the order the caller lists them. Existing configurations with multiple distinct key types may see a one-time in-place reorder in their next plan.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
